    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147">

                <pb facs="0188" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg174"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.415/101: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ciudad Trujillo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-09T14:00:00-05:00">February 9, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>79. I called on Trujillo this morning and informed him orally of contents of
                    Department’s telegram 59.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d147-f1"/> His response was
                    immediate and cordial. In the absence of former [Minister] Franco,<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d147-f2"/> who having been recalled is now in this country, and in
                    view of fact his successor<anchor n="12" xml:id="d147-f3"/> has not yet
                    proceeded to his post, Trujillo called Haitian Minister<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d147-f4"/> to Presidency this afternoon and handed him a letter
                    addressed to President Lescot<anchor n="14" xml:id="d147-f5"/> inviting latter
                    to meet him at frontier to discuss proposal of erecting peace monument in
                    connection with Centennial program. He requested Chevallier to deliver letter
                    personally and immediately to Lescot. Translation of letter follows in my next
                        telegram.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d147-f6"/>
                </p>
                <p>Repeat to Port-au-Prince.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d147-f1" n="10" xml:id="d147-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 9, above.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d147-f2" n="11" xml:id="d147-f2-content">
                <p>Tomás Hernández Franco, Dominican Minister to Haiti.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d147-f3" n="12" xml:id="d147-f3-content">
                <p>Tulio Franco y Franco.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d147-f4" n="13" xml:id="d147-f4-content">
                <p>André Chevallier, Haitian Minister in the Dominican Republic.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d147-f5" n="14" xml:id="d147-f5-content">
                <p>Dated February 9; copy transmitted to the Department in despatch 1552, February
                    9, from Ciudad Trujillo (neither printed).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d147-f6" n="15" xml:id="d147-f6-content">
                <p>Telegram 81, February 9, 7 p.m., not printed.</p>
            </note>
